                <pb facs="0621" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg541"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis reports that the Venezuelan Government protests most strongly against
                    the presence of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Scorpion</hi> in the
                    Orinoco River without having asked permission to enter, declaring such presence
                    to be in violation of Venezuelan as well as of international laws.</p>
                <p>Instructions as to proper reply requested.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
